{"seq":14,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T13:18:00.051Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"a2978391fe44b49ec9a2bb8de349d9fca3b41636e846660502d686aab7412a45","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk (Dock Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through fine. The note also says the kiosk logs need archiving before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (no date). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nSomething to check before this goes in the notes: Marcus's \"Q2 expansion wrap\" note (14 Jul 2025, not one of Moss's) also lists #4419 for QFL, but calls it \"Gate 3 printer lag\" (a BOL printout delay). So one of the two descriptions of #4419 is probably wrong.\n\nThe other QFL notes from Moss (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) have no ticket numbers. The Central handoff note has #4409 and #4412, but those are on Pree's dealer account, not QFL. Also, the cheat sheet points out that Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\") is a different company and isn't a customer, so nothing from it is in this list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
